  "question": {
    "text": "The mean of n items is X . If the first item is increased by 1 , second by 2 and so on, the new mean is :",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "wT6qJ",
      "text": "$\\bar{X}+\\frac{x}{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "aneRW",
      "text": "$\\bar{X}+x$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    },
    {
      "id": "IaCFQ",
      "text": "$\\overline{\\mathrm{X}}+\\frac{\\mathrm{n}+1}{2}$",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": true
    },
    {
      "id": "Y97nh",
      "text": "None of these",
      "image": null,
      "isCorrect": false
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let the items be $\\mathrm{a}_1, \\mathrm{a}_2, \\ldots \\ldots . ., \\mathrm{a}_{\\mathrm{n}}$\nthen $\\bar{X}=\\frac{a_1+a_2+\\ldots \\ldots .+a_n}{n}$\nNow, according to the given condition:\n$\\bar{X}=\\frac{\\left(a_1+1\\right)+\\left(a_2+2\\right)+\\ldots \\ldots \\ldots+\\left(a_n+n\\right)}{n}$\n$=\\overline{\\mathrm{X}}+\\frac{1+2+3+\\ldots \\ldots \\ldots+n}{n}=\\bar{X}+\\frac{n(n+1)}{2 n}$\n(using sum of n natural nos.)\n$=\\overline{\\mathrm{X}}+\\frac{\\mathrm{n}+1}{2}$.",
    "image": null
  },
